   "priceMinor": 50000,
   "currency": "USD",
   "availability": "in_stock",
   "description": "Our watch is a tribute to that spark of blue that lit up the Mississippi Delta and grew to inspire rock 'n roll. The royal blue sunburst dial and the black bezel are stunning combinations that always look sharp. This Swiss-made watch is built for musicians (and fans). It features a unique (patent-pending) bi-directional ceramic bezel emblazoned with the Circle of Fifths. We've even added a unique micro-adjusting clasp that makes it quick and easy to flip the watch around so you can read it no matter how you hold your instrument. This makes this watch a helpful tool for any musician. And any musician will tell you that their instrument takes a beating. The Delta Blue watch is designed to hold up too. Not only is the band and case back made with 316L stainless steel, but the crystal is a durable sapphire. Combine that with 100m of water resistance; this watch is built to last. The Delta Blue Troubadour watch is more than a tool. It's a beautiful piece of jewelry. You can appreciate the fine detail when you view the ETA 2824-2 automatic movement through the exhibition case back. This watch is an excellent gift for any musician or blues fan. Learn more about all the features of the Delta Blue watch below.",
